&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Date: &lt;/strong&gt;Thursday, November 6th, 2025, from 12:30-2:00pm EST&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Zoom&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Series:&lt;/strong&gt; Religion, Culture, and Public Life&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Speakers:&lt;/strong&gt; Aftab Jassal (University of California, San Diego) and Rajbir Singh Judge (California State University, Long Beach)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Moderator&lt;/strong&gt;: Seth Kimmel&amp;nbsp; (Columbia University)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Topics at the intersection of religion, culture, and public life have taken on special urgency in our current moment of social and political upheaval. Join us for an online conversation with recent IRCPL list authors to reflect on what scholarship has looked like in recent years, and to think together about where it could or should head in the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Free and open to the public&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScuJBb3JPfyPaTXscHVaZAlUt4d8tOUMVLXneLX3MPYHpIKYQ/viewform?usp=sharing&amp;amp;ouid=117074755147106152024" target="_blank"&gt;Register here&lt;/a&gt;. The Zoom link will be sent the morning of the event.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the real world, many of the most important negotiations happen when you don&amp;rsquo;t have the final say. Whether you&amp;rsquo;re a mid-level leader, a project manager, a consultant, or an advocate, you often find yourself needing to influence outcomes without holding the formal authority to decide. How do you make progress when the budget, the title, or the board seat isn&amp;rsquo;t yours?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drawing on decades of experience in leadership transitions, community transformation, and C-suite coaching, Reese Fayde will share practical strategies for mapping power dynamics, building coalitions, and reframing issues to align with decision-makers&amp;rsquo; priorities. With real-world stories and actionable tools, this webinar will help you turn &amp;ldquo;no&amp;rdquo; into &amp;ldquo;not yet,&amp;rdquo; create momentum for your ideas, and become an indispensable voice at the table&amp;mdash;even when it&amp;rsquo;s not your table.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
